From eecf05fbbe1e07b1bbf551d7c44afda4b29be96d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noah Cylich <noahcylich@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:20:05 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] temporal-MoE CUDA: released-model routing (decode-time
 residency and Skliar's cache), real-text replay in llama-bench

LLAMA_TEMPORAL_ROUTE=decode follows analysis/residency/decode_state.py: prompt batches are routed
freely while the rule runs observe-only over them, then one rule step per generated token.
LLAMA_TEMPORAL_ROUTE=skliar follows analysis/residency/cache_bias.py: LRU cache of C experts per
layer, lambda times the running mean of max-min logit added to cached experts, top-1 guarantee,
prompt observed unbiased. Both run in one kernel (k_route2) that also keeps the K VRAM slots with
one shared slot routine and starts the copies at the router. TEMPORAL_ROUTE_NOCOPY=1/2 are the
timing controls. Exit line temporal-route2 with the loads histogram; LLAMA_TEMPORAL_ROUTE_DUMP2
writes logits and ids for the routing check. llama-bench replays real tokens from
TEMPORAL_BENCH_CTX/GEN. qwen35moe: TEMPORAL_SHEXP_FIRST=1 orders the shared expert first.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c      |   3 +
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/temporal.cu    | 365 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/models/qwen35moe.cpp          |  22 +-
 tools/llama-bench/llama-bench.cpp |  29 +++
 4 files changed, 414 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

